  "summary": "Massive stone-walled structures with distinctive D-shaped rooms and planned layouts, representing advanced urban planning in pre-Columbian North America.",
  "description": "Features multi-story stone buildings with carefully planned layouts, featuring D-shaped rooms, plazas, and road systems connecting outliers. Developed by ancestral Pueblo peoples during the Chacoan period, reflecting complex social and religious organization.",
  "culturalContext": "Ancestral Puebloan Great Houses — Chaco Canyon's Pueblo Bonito (800-1150 CE, UNESCO) — are the American Southwest's monumental architecture: multi-story planned complexes of 600+ rooms, D-shaped cores, ceremonial kivas (round sunken chambers), aligned to solar-lunar cycles, connected by 400+ km of engineered Chacoan roads. Masonry styles (Type I-II-III) date construction; descendent Pueblo nations (Hopi, Zuni, Taos) keep the cultural lineage, and archaeoastronomy (Supernova pictograph, sun dagger) made Chaco World Heritage.",
